  Q(e^{2pi*i/n}) = i*cot(pi/n)  -- PURELY IMAGINARY for all n >= 2.
  |Q| = |cot(pi/n)| = cos(pi/n)/sin(pi/n).

  Notable values:
    n=2: Q(-1) = 0     (the zero, t=-1 is the 'Alexander' point)
    n=3: Q(omega_3) = i*cot(pi/3) = i/sqrt(3) = i*0.5774...
    n=4: Q(i) = i*cot(pi/4) = i*1 = i
    n=6: Q(omega_6) = i*cot(pi/6) = i*sqrt(3) = i*1.7321...

